  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">NCDPZ - EC Urban Livelihoods Protection and Promotion Programme</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The complex emergency that Zimbabwe is slowly emerging from has led to limited access to basic goods and services, high prevalence of disease, and collapse of basic infrastructure. High unemployment and the effects of HIV and AIDS have exacerbated poverty in urban areas. Political instability and tensions have also jeopardized livelihoods of the urban populace. For this action, CAFOD and NCDPZ protect and promote urban livelihoods of the vulnerable and poor people through focussing on the following key interventions;

1) Unconditional Cash transfers
2)Internal Savings and Lending Schemes
3)Micro-grants
4)WASH activities 
5)Community home based care</narrative>
  </description>
